      "math_academy_id": "q-184131",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Suppose $n=-10b-5,$ where $b\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is odd.\n\nThe number $n$ is odd since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =-10b-5 \\\\  & =2({{field-1}})+1 \\\\  & ={{field-2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=$ {{field-3}}, which is an integer.",
